From f96d9fcaf2537c94410a44a7df7bbe17f642b4f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:08:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] VAX8200: DEBNA VAXBI Ethernet adapter (device ET, node 7)

The DEBNA's BI VAX Port (BVP) Ethernet port: BIIC node with DTYPE 410F,
node reset and self-test (BROKE while testing), port registers PC/PS/PE/PD
at node space 204-210, PUDR, the Ethernet address at 218-21D.  Port
instructions INIT (PQB), ENABLE, SHUTDOWN, command and free queue
notices; the PQB, free queue block and buffer descriptor table in host
memory, self-relative interlocked queues reached by system virtual
address (vax_bi_dma.c); messages (system ID, parameters, counters,
protocol type definition blocks), transmit and receive datagrams through
sim_ether, the interrupt vector from the PQB.
Disabled by default.

VMS V4.7 configures it ("BI - AIE Adapter with NI port only", ETA0,
DECnet line BNT-0); DECnet to a MicroVAX II (DELQA) over a UDP link:
copies, SET HOST, NCP LOOP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
